SUMMARY:Ali Wong Live LIVE at McCaw Hall (Aug 13)
DTSTAMP:20260812T042858Z
DTSTART:20260813T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate l
	inks. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout Ali Wong\n
	Ali Wong is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians of her generatio
	n\, known for her fearlessly raw\, hilarious\, and unapologetically honest
	 comedy style. She burst into mainstream consciousness with her Netflix sp
	ecials Baby Cobra (2016) and Hard Knock Wife (2018)\, both filmed while sh
	e was visibly pregnant — a bold and unforgettable choice that became her s
	ignature image. \nHer comedy dives deep into marriage\, motherhood\, sex\,
	 race\, and the absurdities of modern life\, delivered with a rapid-fire w
	it and zero filter. Wong’s ability to make audiences simultaneously cringe
	 and howl with laughter has earned her a devoted global fanbase and critic
	al acclaim across the entertainment industry. \nBeyond stand-up\, Ali Wong
	 has starred in the hit Netflix romantic comedy film Always Be My Maybe (2
	019)\, the critically acclaimed drama series Beef (2023) — for which she w
	on a Primetime Emmy Award — and has appeared in numerous television and fi
	lm projects. Her live shows are known for being high-energy\, deeply perso
	nal\, and absolutely unforgettable. \nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\, Augu
	st 13\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM \nVenue: McCaw Hall\, 321 Mercer Street\, Sea
	ttle\, WA 98109 \nTicket Price Range: $59 – $199 \nAge Restrictions: This 
	is an 18+ show. Strong adult language and mature themes throughout. \nAbou
	t McCaw Hall\nMarion Oliver McCaw Hall is one of Seattle’s premier perform
	ing arts venues\, located in the heart of the Seattle Center campus — just
	 steps from the iconic Space Needle. The hall is home to the Seattle Opera
	 and Pacific Northwest Ballet\, and regularly hosts world-class comedy\, m
	usic\, and special events. \nWith a seating capacity of approximately 2\,9
	00\, McCaw Hall offers excellent sightlines from virtually every seat in t
	he house. The venue features a stunning modern design with state-of-the-ar
	t acoustics\, comfortable seating\, and a welcoming atmosphere that makes 
	every performance feel intimate despite its size. \nAmenities include mult
	iple bars and concession areas\, accessible seating options\, and convenie
	nt parking in the Seattle Center garage. The surrounding Seattle Center gr
	ounds offer great pre-show dining and entertainment options\, making it ea
	sy to turn the evening into a full night out. \nWhat to Expect\nAli Wong’s
	 live shows are a masterclass in stand-up comedy — fast-paced\, deeply per
	sonal\, and packed with laugh-out-loud moments from start to finish. Expec
	t her signature blend of self-deprecating humor\, sharp social commentary\
	, and stories about relationships\, family\, and the chaos of everyday lif
	e. \nThis is a solo stand-up performance\, so you’ll get the full Ali Wong
	 experience with no distractions. Fans of her Netflix specials will recogn
	ize her style but can expect all-new material crafted for this tour. Arriv
	e early to grab a drink\, find your seat\, and soak in the energy of a sol
	d-out crowd ready to laugh. \nShows typically run approximately 75–90 minu
	tes with no intermission. Dress comfortably — this is a casual\, fun night
	 out with one of comedy’s biggest stars. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range
	: $59 – $199 (plus applicable fees) \nTickets are available through Ticket
	master (official) and VividSeats (resale marketplace). Resale ticket price
	s may vary from face value. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post c
	ontains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
	\n\nhttps://comedycalendar.com/event/ali-wong-live-at-mccaw-hall-aug-thu/\
	n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/ali-wong-live-at-mccaw-hall-aug-thu/
